5809495,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.07252486194267155,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01446,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":9.6,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"SoFi Technologies, Inc. provides various financial services in the United States, Latin America, Canada, and Hong Kong. The company operates through three segments: Lending, Technology Platform, and Financial Services. It offers lending and financial services and products that allows its members to borrow, save, spend, invest, and protect money; and personal loans, student loans, home loans, and related services. The company also operates Galileo, a technology platform that offers services to financial and non-financial institution; and Technisys, a cloud-native digital and core banking platform that provides software licenses and associated services, including implementation and maintenance. In addition, it provides SoFi Money offers checking and savings accounts, and cash management products; SoFi Invest, a mobile-first investment platform that offers access to trading and advisory solutions, such as investing and robo-advisory; and SoFI Crypto, a new digital asset trading platform. Further, the company offers SoFi Credit Card that provides cash back rewards on every purchase; Sofi Relay, a personal finance management product that allows to track all of their financial accounts comprising credit score and spending behaviors; SoFi Protect which offers insurance product; SoFi Travel, an application that manages travel search and booking experience; SoFi At Work provides financial benefits to employees, including student loan payments made on their employees' behalf; Lantern Credit, a financial services marketplace platform for seeking alternative products and provide product comparisons; and other lending as a service that offers pre-qualified borrower referrals and offers loans to third-party partner. The company was founded in 2011 and is based in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Anthony J. Noto | CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $5.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 6K people. Revenue per employee of $592K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 38%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $43K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["SoFi Technologies, Inc. is a large-cap financial services business with a $21.0B market cap on $3.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +32% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -4% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $4.0B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +8.3% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 15.2% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (17.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Financial Services peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 15% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +8.3% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Growing faster than most Financial Services peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"SoFi Technologies (NASDAQ:SOFI) Shares Climb 1.1% \u2013 Time to Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/sofi-technologies-nasdaqsofi-shares-climb-1-1-time-to-buy.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794004876.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.836,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"SoFi Stock Is Down 50% From Its High. Here's Why